            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KissTheChefette"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow. This is amazing. I used 6oz of pineapple juice, about 8oz of mango rum and 3 ounces of mango juice, no sugar and 3 scoops of vanilla ice cream (no heavy cream) This is quite possibly the best adult beverage I've ever had in my life! THANK YOU!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Danigirl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really good. Our big blender broke so we just have a smoothie maker. So I made this at a much smaller scale. With 3/4 cup pineapple juice, about 5 frozen mango chunks, 5 large ice cubes, 2 tbs of cream of coconut, 1 scoop of vanilla ice cream, 1/2 cup coconut milk and 1 shot of coconut white rum. It was delicious and both my fiancé and I loved it!",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-06T18:39:23.207Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Viv"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Amazing. Tastes EXACTLY like a virgin pina colada. Made for 2 people. CHANGES MADE: used 1 teaspoon of stevia (instead of white sugar). Omitted the cream altogether but used a full can of coconut milk. Used a whole mango. WOW!",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-23T21:18:12.250Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "n_ali514"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummmmmmmm! This was so yummy! I reduced the pine apple juice quantity to 1 cup, crushed some of the ice before adding the other ingredients along with the remaining ice cubes. Finally, I topped it off with whipped cream and it tasted amazing! The taste was VERY similar to the mango pinacolada I had at a mexican restaurant!",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-31T12:54:47.387Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kirsten Kennelly Cone"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Pretty good! We used agave and skim milk instead of sugar and heavy cream. It hit the spot on a hot day.",
            "datePublished": "2015-01-24T13:47:05.440Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sueb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am rating this on inspiration, not as the recipe is written. I used a mango, forgot about the ice cubes (didn't have the recipe in front of me), omitted the sugar, used 1 1/4 cups of freshly cut pineapple, 1/2 cup soy milk, and 1/2 cup freshly made coconut milk. It was fantastic! It was a great start to my day!",
            "datePublished": "2010-07-19T14:28:56.940Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "S Javon Stokely"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My true critics (children) liked it and asked for seconds. It didn't give me a wow factor but It was still good. ( I was still full from dinner). This was my first time working with coconut milk and I loved the creamy texture. I'll definitely give this a try again. (Next time I will use a fresh Mango instead of frozen)",
            "datePublished": "2018-03-08T16:03:23.977Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sulaiman Khan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great Smootie!!! I used plain and vanilla yogurt instead of heavy cream. Also I made 2 smoothies: one with coconut milk, and one with coconut water. I made them for my family and they liked the milk one much more. I personally liked the water more though. You can make this with either recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-27T16:59:52.257Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KERI KENNELLY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Absolutely delicious!! I used frozen mango, no ice and 1% milk instead of cream. The flavor was fantasic and it was rich and creamy. :) Will probably make these one evening and add some vodka, but will Definitely be making these again as is with brunch! :)",
            "datePublished": "2009-08-16T12:46:09.630Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ms Jean"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used a handful of frozen mango and also added a frozen banana. It had a good, thick consistency. Maybe that's because I didn't add the heavy cream. I don't usually have that on hand, but I'd probably replace it with half-N-half or milk anyway. It was plenty sweet with only a half packet of Stevia. I'm sure a little rum would make this even better! Thanks for the recipe, Godiva Goddess!",
            "datePublished": "2014-06-06T07:21:01.033Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naples34102"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Mmmmmm-mm! The aroma of this alone is intoxicating and inviting. Once you take that first sip you get exactly what you were signaled to expect - a rich but refreshing, creamy, pastel-colored, not too sweet drink that reminds you of a chaise lounge, pool and sunshine. I used Splenda rather than sugar and half-and-half rather than cream but beyond that, stuck to the recipe. I generally make Hubs his preferred yogurt-based smoothies but for me today, this was a refreshing and welcome change. Normally I might garnish this like a Pina Colada - a wedge of pineapple perhaps, a maraschino cherry and a paper umbrella of course, but this time we just slurped this up straight out of the blender, the two of us cleaning up this \"4-serving\" recipe in no time. Loved it.",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-19T07:06:11.403Z"
          },
          {
